  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,4\\})+P(X=5) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =F(5)-F(4) \\\\  & =0.1912-0.0996 \\\\  & =0.0916.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
